\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Where this paper sits. The L0$\to $L3 stack (ADR-0048): each rung serves a different \emph  {whom}, and each announces what it assumes from below. Papers 1--3 climb L2, L0/L1, and the L3 identity bridge respectively; \emph  {The Harbor Economy} is the top rung --- the only layer whose participants are plural and mutually distrusting. It consumes the BUILT bond ledger from L0, the cryptographic \texttt  {auth-chain} from L1, and the legible \emph  {person} from Paper~3, and turns them into a market. The vertical arrow is the volume's spine: the same memory that makes the single-player wedge good is what turns a spawn into a tradeable asset.}}{4}{figure.caption.2}\protected@file@percent }
